<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Klein Vrystaat</h1><p class="st-meta">1886 CE – 1891 CE · capital Piet Retief</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Boer republic on the Swazi border, created from a land grant by the Swazi king Mbandzeni.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1886 a group of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> farmers who had obtained grazing and land concessions from the Swazi king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbandzeni">Mbandzeni</a> in the southwest of his kingdom set themselves up as an independent republic, the Little Free State, around the area of the later town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-retief">Piet Retief</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is recorded beyond its small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad-dutch-east-indies">Volksraad</a> and a population of a few dozen farming families. Its existence was one example of the concessions that left much of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom">Swazi Kingdom</a> in the hands of outsiders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Klein Vrystaat was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a> in 1891.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/klein-vrystaat.jpg" alt="Klein Vrystaat" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Great Brightstar and others · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Klein_Vrystaat_-_2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1886 CE – 1891 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Piet Retief</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Little Free State</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1888&amp;focus=klein-vrystaat" aria-label="Klein Vrystaat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5491 3168 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Klein Vrystaat lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5811 3424L5823 3405M5811 3424L5746 3380"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5823 3405h0M5746 3380h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5811 3424h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5811 3424h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Piet Retief. <a href="/atlas?year=1888&amp;focus=klein-vrystaat">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
